{
  "manufacturer": "Laars",
  "manufacturer_slug": "laars",
  "model": "Multiburner control - ProtoNode",
  "model_slug": "multiburner-protonode",
  "aliases": [
    "Multiburner",
    "Laars Multiburner",
    "Multi-burner",
    "ProtoNode FPC-N34",
    "ProtoNode FPC-N35",
    "FPC-N34-0701",
    "Laars ProtoNode"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler controller gateway",
  "applies_to": "Laars boilers with the Multiburner control, read through a ProtoNode FPC-N34 gateway (the document does not name the models).",
  "summary": "The ProtoNode reads the Multiburner control over Modbus RTU and serves 149 objects per boiler. Analog inputs cover temperatures, flame signals, fan and blower speeds, lockout and blocking codes, history counters and lead-lag slave states; binary inputs show the safety chain switches, contacts and gas valve stages. Writable AVs and BVs hold the CH1-CH4, DHW and cascade enables, setpoints and PID terms plus the demand switches.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "50000 + device Node-ID",
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Each boiler on the ProtoNode's RS-485 bus shows up as its own BACnet device, and every one uses the same object IDs. The device instance is Node_Offset (default 50000) plus the boiler's Node-ID, so Node-ID 1 = device 50001.",
    "The mapping has no read/write column. AV, BV and MV objects are mapped to Metasys N2 outputs and LonWorks input variables, so they are listed here as writable; AI, BI and MI objects are read-only.",
    "No units or state texts are given; the LonWorks SNVT types show which values are temperatures, percentages and hours.",
    "Bit-mapped binary inputs are numbered from their Modbus register and bit: BI 1800-1807 are register 40018 bits 0-7, BI 2100-2108 are register 40021 bits 0-8, and so on.",
    "Points named '/ 10' (call-for-heat and cycle counts) are reported divided by 10."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Enable the CH1 circuit, give it a call for heat with BV 1 and write the CH1 setpoint (or the cascade setpoint when boilers run in cascade). Read the run contact, burner 1 status and outlet temperature, and watch the alarm contact and lockout code.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 0",
        "name": "CH1 enable/disable",
        "why": "CH1 heating circuit enable"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "CH1 demand",
        "why": "CH1 call for heat"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "CH1 setpoint",
        "why": "CH1 water setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 27",
        "name": "Cascade setpoint",
        "why": "Setpoint when boilers run in cascade"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 2100",
        "name": "Boiler Run Contact",
        "why": "Boiler run output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 84",
        "name": "Burner 1 status",
        "why": "Burner 1 state code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Outlet Temp",
        "why": "Outlet water temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 2101",
        "name": "Alarm Contact",
        "why": "Alarm output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "Lockout Code",
        "why": "Lockout reason code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "AV 0 CH1 enable/disable enables the CH1 circuit and BV 1 CH1 demand is its call for heat; the mapping gives no values for either. CH2-CH4 and DHW have matching enable, setpoint and demand objects.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Device instance = Node_Offset + boiler Node-ID. Node_Offset defaults to 50000 and is changed in the ProtoNode web configurator; Node-IDs must be unique, 1-255.",
      "Boiler to ProtoNode: Modbus RTU, 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit.",
      "Default ProtoNode IP address 192.168.1.24, mask 255.255.255.0. Choose BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP with the Protocol Selector, then add one profile per device with its Node-ID.",
      "With more than one device on a ProtoNode, set BACnet Virtual Server Nodes to Yes. For BACnet MS/TP also set MAC address, baud rate and Max Master.",
      "Two or more ProtoNodes on the same subnet need different BACnet Network Numbers (default 50).",
      "A ProtoNode handles 1,500 registers in total; this profile uses 149 per device."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The PID terms (P, I, D) for every circuit are writable AVs; they are tuning values, not points to write from a BMS.",
      "No code lists are given for Lockout Code, Blocking Code or the burner and slave states.",
      "BV 5 Parameters enable is writable but not explained in the mapping."
    ]
  },
  "source": {
